.TH WM2-SWIPE 1 "2026-10-23" "wm2tj 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wm2-swipe \- switch virtual desktops with a three-finger touchpad swipe
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wm2-swipe
.RB [ \-f
.IR fingers ]
.RB [ \-t
.IR threshold ]
.RB [ \-r ]
.RB [ \-w ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wm2-swipe
waits for touchpad swipe gestures and switches to the next or previous
virtual desktop.  It reads the X server's own XInput 2.4 gesture events,
which Xorg 21 and later deliver for libinput touchpads, so it needs no root
privileges and no membership of the
.I input
group.  The switch is requested through the EWMH property
.BR _NET_CURRENT_DESKTOP ,
so it works with
.BR wm2tj (1)
and with any other EWMH window manager.
.PP
By default a swipe to the right goes to the next desktop and a swipe to the
left to the previous one, and nothing happens at the first or last desktop.
.B wm2-session
starts it when it is installed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-f " fingers"
Number of fingers of the swipe (default 3).
.TP
.BI \-t " threshold"
Minimum horizontal travel, in libinput's unaccelerated motion units, before
a swipe counts (default 60).  Shorter swipes, and swipes that move more
vertically than horizontally, are ignored.
.TP
.B \-r
Reverse the direction: a swipe to the left goes to the next desktop, as in
GNOME and macOS.
.TP
.B \-w
Wrap around: the next desktop after the last one is the first.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
"the X server has no XInput 2.4 gestures": the X server is older than
Xorg 21, or the session does not run on Xorg.  "gesture grab failed": another
program already grabs the swipe gestures;
.B wm2-swipe
then still listens on the root window, but applications that use gestures
themselves may take the swipe first.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wm2tj (1),
.BR libinput (4)
